Content: BEAD Program
Tennessee's BEAD (Broadband Equity, Access, and Deployment) Program

Overview
Tennessee has been allocated $683,057,831 in BEAD funding to expand broadband access to unserved and underserved locations across the state.

Program Status
Tennessee's BEAD Initial Proposal has been approved by NTIA. The state is now progressing through the subgrantee selection process.

Eligible Entities
Eligible subgrantees include:
- Internet service providers (ISPs)
- Municipal utilities and electric cooperatives
- Local governments
- Other eligible entities

Priority Areas
The program prioritizes deployment to unserved locations (no broadband service at 25/3 Mbps or faster) and underserved locations (no broadband service at 100/20 Mbps or faster).

Timeline
- Initial Proposal: Approved
- Final Proposal: In progress
- Subgrantee Selection: Expected 2025-2026
- Deployment: 2026-2030

For more information, visit connecttn.org or contact ConnectTN at info@connecttn.org.
</tool_response>

